  "independent_methods": {
    "XIV_layout": "Stub m; main columns0..9 and separate italic correction columns1..9, repeated at the bottom. PDF69 rows,00..,34; PDF70 ,35..,69; PDF71 ,70..,99. This is layout observation, not certification of all cells.",
    "XIV_lookup": "For x=n+f with n=floor(x) and 0<=f<1, take row from the first two fractional digits and main column from the third. Add the same-row right-hand correction for the fourth fractional digit, if nonzero. The printed integer plus correction gives four significant digits; its f-only value is that integer divided by1000. Multiply by10^n. Zero fourth digit requires no correction lookup.",
    "decimal_placement_basis": "N35 already-PASS prose: 0.046 -> row0.04/main6 ->1112 ->1.112 because1<10^0.046<10; 0.0467 adds correction7=2 ->1.114; -2.685=-3+0.315 ->2.065*10^-3. The general floor decomposition follows ordinary exponent laws; it is not invented wording attributed to 2010.",
    "PDF71_original_method": "The paragraph first describes TableXIII: first two significant digits choose the row, third the main column, fourth the same-row italic correction; the correction is added. Its XIII example is3174 ->5011+6=5017. It then says TableXIV is used similarly to obtain a number from the given logarithm mantissa:8352 ->6839+3=6842. Decimal-sign position is determined by the characteristic.",
    "PDF71_scope_limit": "The 2010 paragraph itself only states characteristic determines the decimal position; it does not itself restate N35's 0.046/0.0467 examples or floor decomposition of negative exponents. Those valid lesson/mathematical steps are independently sourced above; absence of repetition is not a global HOLD.",
    "IV_required_route": "Reuse source-only IV rules and previously independently audited cells. Square roots are four-significant-digit values. Normalize using even powers of10; shifting a radicand by2k decimal places shifts the root byk. For0.1 use0.1=10*10^-2, so sqrt0.1 is the read sqrt10 cell divided by10. No new correction is required for the three exact grid radicands.",
    "table_vs_calculation": "Printed main cells and correction integers below came from pixels or explicit unchanged PASS source-cell reuse, never Math.pow/Math.sqrt. Arithmetic on those cells and deterministic high-precision sanity calculations are separately labelled. Rounded table interpolation need not equal a freshly computed and directly rounded transcendental value."
  },
